# Rust
target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# OpenAI / secrets. Keep this list broad: the whole `.env.*` family and the
# direnv pair habitually carry OPENAI_API_KEY, and a new `.env.<stage>` must
# be ignored the day someone creates it, not the day someone remembers to
# add it here. Committed examples are un-ignored one by one below — extend
# that allow-list, never narrow `.env.*`.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.*.example
.envrc
.direnv/
*.api_key
profiles/local-*.toml

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo

# Local Claude permission overrides
.claude/settings.local.json

# JS / web demo build artifacts
node_modules/
dist/
.cache/
# Track C wasm module — regenerate with scripts/build-wasm.sh (ADR-0019).
web/wasm/
# …and the siblings its staged publish renames through (.wasm.staging.*,
# .wasm.backup.*, .wasm.publish.lock). They exist only for the length of one
# build and are removed on every exit path, but a `kill -9` mid-build leaves
# one behind, and residue from a build has no business showing up as an
# untracked file in a concurrent session's status.
web/.wasm.*

# Test outputs
out/
*.tmp.md
*.tmp.json

# Korean translation sidecars (out of scope for the assistant; managed by
# external translation tooling)
*.ko.md

# Committed lockfile — the known-good resolution satisfying the wasm-bindgen
# exact pin (owner decision 2026-08-06, oi-0020); overrides the machine-global
# ignore. CLAUDE.md stays ignored by the same owner decision.
!Cargo.lock

# Analysis bundles — generated snapshots of this tree, not authored docs.
# `docs/investigation/` was committed on 2026-08-06 as a dated record (727d3bc,
# owner decision A-4); the owner reversed that on 2026-08-08 and it is untracked
# again. The files stay on disk — only their tracking is withdrawn — because
# they are regenerated from the code rather than edited by hand, so every
# regeneration produced a diff that carried no decision. `reviews/` is untracked
# for the same reason.
docs/investigation/
